Track 1: Taproots Drink the Battery
- Story & Context: The genre's chaotic birth was captured during a blackout performance beneath the high-voltage lines outside St. Jude’s Sanatorium, where Brother Kael first ran an amp directly off a stolen diesel generator. Mara Yipirinya plugged her contact-miked didgeridoo into a modular rig running a transcribed night-terror patch, causing the power grid to surge and triggering a spontaneous street riot. The track records the moment security gates were breached, caught over a stomping 110 BPM dembow pulse. Kael screamed over the distorted sub-frequencies, establishing the scene's battle cry: "Unplug the altar, let the timber bleed!"
