Track 2: Callus & Kambium
- Story & Context: Recorded in a single unedited take in the humid basement of a abandoned botanical nursery, this confession piece details Mara’s complete break from mainstream electropop production after being blacklisted by label executives. She channels her isolation into a barrage of throat-singing overtones and harsh vocal chops, targeting the corporate machine that commodified her culture. The track relies on a relentless, stuttering moombahton kick pattern overlaid with screaming synth leads, building into a cathartic vocal breakdown. Mara spits her refusal to conform, growling the hook: "You bought the flower but you feared the thorn!"
