Track 3: The Wardens of Scion House
- Story & Context: The legendary aftermath track memorializes the night the Abbaye de Saint-Wandrille cellar was permanently sealed by municipal authorities after three hundred revelers danced until the floorboards collapsed into the catacombs. Built around a slow-burning, ominous Phrygian drone transcribed from the oldest monastic sleep logs, the song evolves into a euphoric, aggressive anthem of underground resilience. It ends with the recorded sound of rain hitting cathedral leadwork as the synth patches slowly decay into static. The final crowd chant echoes through the reverb tail: "What we buried in the limestone will grow back through the floor!"
